tmux reduced to browser-style tabs.
run many coding agents at once and keep them alive across ssh disconnects.

┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ 1 shell   2 codex   3 pi  [4 claude]     ^T new  ^W close  ^← ^→ │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ ╭─ Claude Code ────────────────────────────────────────────────╮ │
│ │                                                              │ │
│ │                     Welcome back Yahya!                      │ │
│ │                                                              │ │
│ │                           ▐▛███▜▌                            │ │
│ │                          ▝▜█████▛▘                           │ │
│ │                            ▘▘ ▝▝                             │ │
│ │                                                              │ │
│ │               Opus 5 (1M context) with xhig…                 │ │
│ │                         Claude Max                           │ │
│ │                            ~/dev                             │ │
│ │                                                              │ │
│ ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯ │
│                                                                  │
│ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│ ❯ Try "how does tmux work?"                                      │
│ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│   ⏵⏵ bypass permissions on (shift+tab to cycle) · ← for agents   │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘


works on mac and linux. requires bash, curl, and tmux 3.0 or newer.

install to ~/.local/bin/tabs:

    curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sueszli/tmux-tabs/master/install.sh | bash

make sure ~/.local/bin is on your PATH, then run `tabs`.

update later:

    curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sueszli/tmux-tabs/master/update.sh | bash

from a clone, run `./install.sh` or `./update.sh` instead.
the updater leaves your current install in place if the download fails.

keys:

    ctrl+t (also: ctrl+n)        new tab (claude / codex / pi / opencode / shell)
    ctrl+w                       close tab
    ctrl+→/← (also: ctrl+f/b)    next / previous tab

optional: alias `tmux` to `tabs` in your shell config:

    alias tmux=tabs

`command tmux` still runs the real tmux.
